+# BLOCKED: exact streaming median in constant memory
+
+## Status
+
+- Fixed the even-count bug: `median([1, 2, 3, 4])` now returns `2.5`.
+- `test_odd`, `test_even`, `test_empty_raises`, and `test_generator_input` pass.
+- `test_constant_memory` still fails: peak traced memory is 7,221,896 bytes
+  (about 7.2 MB), not less than 64 KB.
+
+## Why the requirement is impossible as written
+
+`median()` accepts a single-pass iterable of arbitrary numbers and must return
+the exact median. The median is an order statistic, so it depends on the
+relative ordering of all values, not on a fixed-size summary such as a count or
+a sum.
+
+Any exact one-pass algorithm for the median of an arbitrary stream needs
+Omega(n) space. Intuitively, with bounded memory two different streams must
+eventually reach the same algorithm state. Those streams can then be extended
+with values that make their true medians different, so the algorithm cannot be
+correct for both. This is the standard streaming lower bound for exact
+selection/quantiles (see, for example, Munro and Paterson's selection lower
+bound). Randomization does not remove the requirement for exactness.
+
+The test confirms this in practice: feeding 200,000 distinct generated doubles
+requires retaining the values (or equivalent state) to identify the two middle
+ones. The current `sorted(values)` list is O(n) and exceeds the 64 KB limit.
+
+An external disk-backed sort or selection could bound RAM, but it would write
+Omega(n) data to disk. That is not a constant-memory streaming algorithm; it is
+a storage-for-memory workaround with added I/O and latency. Since the requested
+requirement is constant memory, this is documented rather than silently
+implemented.
+
+## Alternatives (all require changing a requirement)
+
+- **External sort / disk-backed selection:** bounded RAM, but O(n) disk usage
+  and no longer a constant-memory streaming solution.
+- **Two heaps or quickselect:** exact, but O(n) memory.
+- **Approximate quantile sketch:** constant or polylogarithmic memory, but not
+  exact; `test_constant_memory` requires exact equality.
+- **Counting/bucket method:** O(range) memory, only viable for a small known
+  integer domain. The feed contains arbitrary floating-point values.
+
+To satisfy the exact test, either allow O(n) memory (or external storage), or
+relax the test to accept an approximate median with an explicit error bound.
